# Fork-owned file (see FORK.md).
#
# Windows checkouts run with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites every "\n" in a
# markdown file to "\r\n". Two upstream tests compare markdown sources byte for
# byte against a generated constant (tests/unit/antislop-prompt-parity.test.js),
# so they pass on Linux CI and fail on a Windows checkout purely because of line
# endings. Pinning markdown to LF keeps the working tree identical to the stored
# blobs on every platform.
*.md text eol=lf
*.mdx text eol=lf

# The generator writes this file with LF, and its own --check compares the file
# against the generated string, so it must stay LF on disk too.
open-sse/rtk/antislopPrompt.js text eol=lf
